==Description==

The [[Image:Silk_Point_onCurve.svg|32px]] '''Silk Point_onCurve''' command creates a point, a Point_onCurve object, on a [[Silk_CubicCurve_4|CubicCurve_4]] or [[Silk_CubicCurve_6|CubicCurve_6]] (also works on some curves outside of Silk).

</translate>
[[File:3.-Point_onCurve.png|300px]]
<translate>

{{Caption|Point_onCurve markers placed along two curves, showing the u parameter}}

==Usage==

# Indicate a point by clicking on the curve in the [[3D_View|3D View]]
# There are several ways to invoke the tool.
#* Press the {{Button|[[Image:Silk_Point_onCurve.svg|16px]] Point onCurve}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|[[Image:Silk_Point_onCurve.svg|16px]] Silk → Point onCurve}} option from the menu.
# A point on the curve, a '''Point_onCurve''' object, is created.

== Properties ==

See also: [[Property_View|Property View]].

A  '''Point_onCurve''' is derived from a [[Part_Feature|Part feature]], or more precise a {{Incode|Part::FeaturePython}} object, and inherits all its properties. It also has the following additional property:

=== Data ===

{{Properties_Title|C1 - Inputs}}

* {{PropertyData|NL_Curve|Link}}: Reference curve.
* {{PropertyData|reverse|Bool}}: Default is {{value|False}}. Reverses the parameter direction.
* {{PropertyData|u|FloatConstraint}}: Parameter along curve.

{{Properties_Title|C2 - Outputs}}

* {{PropertyData|Position|Vector}}: Position vector.

{{Properties_Title|C3 - Identifiers}}

* {{PropertyData|internalName|String}}: The permanent internal FreeCAD name for this object.
* {{PropertyData|object_type|String}}: Default is {{value|Point_onCurve}}. The workbench class used to create this object.
* {{PropertyData|object_version|String}}: The class version of this object.


